.Dd 2018-04-08
.Dt LBTS-INIT 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts init
.Nd create an empty LightBTS instance or reinitialize an existing owner
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts init
.Op Fl -git
.Op Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command creates an empty LightBTS instance - basically a
.Pa .lightbts
directory with subdirectories for
.Pa hooks
and
.Pa messages ,
and the files
.Pa config
and
.Pa index .
.Pp
If the
.Ev LIGHTBTS_DIR
environment variable is set then it will be used instead of
.Pa ./.lightbts
for the base directory of the LightBTS instance.
.Pp
Running
.Nm lbts init
where an instance already exists fails, without changing anything,
unless
.Fl -git
is used to move the instance into git.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -git
Store the instance in the git repository that contains the directory,
in a branch named
.Ql lightbts
that is checked out as a worktree in
.Pa .lightbts
in the top directory of the repository.
If the repository already has that branch, locally or as
.Ql origin/lightbts ,
it is checked out, and the index is built from its messages.
If
.Pa .lightbts
is an instance that is not stored in git yet, its messages and configuration are moved into a new branch.
See
.Xr lbts-sync 1 .
.El
.Pp
If a
.Ar directory
is specified on the command line,
it will use that instead of
.Ev LIGHTBTS_DIR
or
.Pa ./.lightbts .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 .
.Sh AUTHOR
.An "Guus Sliepen" Aq guus@lightbts.info
